  "debug.fantasy_furniture.cabinet.shelf_removed": "Removed cabinet shelf %s",
  "debug.fantasy_furniture.cabinet.shelf_restored": "Restored cabinet shelf %s",
  "message.fantasy_furniture.cabinet.no_capacity": "Not enough space in the cabinet.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.category.hygiene": "Hygiene",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.category.hygiene.desc": "Soap, wrapping, racks, the mold, bottles, and the display cabinet.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.soap_bar": "Right-click the top of a solid block to set it down. It will not float or stick to a wall. The six colors are on the next page.$(br)Leave it in water and it shrinks a little every minute. Take it out and it stops. Once it cannot shrink any more, one more minute in water melts it away and leaves nothing.$(br)Hold the use key in the air. Standing blows bubbles onto your head for ten seconds and does not use the soap. Sneaking does the same for ten minutes and uses one bar, except in Creative. Breaking it drops soap of the same color and size.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.page.soap_bar": "Six colors",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.page.variants": "Variant looks",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.soap_box": "Set it on top of a solid block. Right-click a closed empty box to open the lid; right-click again with an empty hand to close it. With the lid open, right-click while holding soap to put one in; sneak and right-click to take it out.$(br)The brush only changes the box color, not the soap inside. The six looks are on the next page. Creative mode only gives closed empty boxes.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.soap_rack": "Set it on top of a solid block. Right-click an empty rack while holding soap to put one on; sneak and right-click to take it off. The rack has no lid.$(br)You cannot recolor the rack with a brush. It can also sit under a stack of cream, body wash, or shampoo.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.soap_paper_box": "Hold a paper box and right-click unwrapped soap on the ground to wrap it. On a wrapped bar: right-click with an empty hand to switch between closed and open; sneak and right-click to take it back; hold use in your hand to tear the wrap off.$(br)Empty boxes and wrapped bars can stack together, up to seven high. Sneak and right-click to take the top one. The brush only changes the box color. The looks are on the next page.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.soap_paper_bag": "Same as the paper box, but it is a bag: wrap it, open it, sneak to take it back, and hold use in your hand to tear the wrap off. Empty bags and bagged soap can stack together. The brush only changes the bag color, not the soap. The looks are on the next page.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.soap_mold": "Set it on top of a solid block. Right-click to add, in order: one body-wash or shampoo liquid (this sets the color of the particles in water), one honeycomb, one bucket of water (you get the empty bucket back), then one of the six dyes (this sets how the soap looks).$(br)When all four are in, right-click to mix, wait about five seconds, then right-click to take the soap. Before mixing, sneak and right-click to undo the last thing you added. Bottled body wash and shampoo cannot be used as ingredients.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.body_cream": "Right-click the top of a solid block to set it down. It can stack in the same spot with body wash and shampoo, in any order, up to four bottles. If all four are cream, you may add a fifth cream; if any wash or shampoo is in the stack, four is the limit. You can also add onto a stack that is already there, or aim at the block under the stack. The looks are on the next page.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.body_wash": "Right-click the top of a solid block to set it down. It can stack with cream and shampoo, in any order, up to four bottles; if any wash or shampoo is in the stack, four is the limit. You can also add onto a stack that is already there. An open display cabinet that is not full will take one.$(br)Soap is made with the liquid, not this bottle. The looks are on the next page.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.shampoo": "Right-click the top of a solid block to set it down. It can stack with cream and body wash, in any order, up to four bottles; if any wash or shampoo is in the stack, four is the limit. You can also add onto a stack that is already there. An open display cabinet that is not full will take one.$(br)Soap is made with the liquid, not this bottle. The looks are on the next page.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.display_cabinet": "Right-click the top of a solid block to set it down. Right-click to open or close the door. While it is open and not full, right-click with body wash or shampoo to put one bottle in.$(br)Wash and shampoo together can be at most two bottles. The looks are on the next page.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.category.building": "Building",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.category.building.desc": "Tiles, wallpaper, wainscot, the screen, styled windows, and stairs.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.category.furniture": "Furniture",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.category.furniture.desc": "Sofas, cabinets, computers, bookshelves, bedding, drinkware, and other furniture.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.decorative_screen": "Right-click to set it down. It is two blocks tall, and it faces the way you are looking. You bump into the thin side, but light passes through.$(br)Right-clicking it again does nothing. You cannot recolor it or store anything in it. Breaking either half drops the whole screen as one item.",
  "block.fantasy_furniture.sofa_1": "Sofa Type 1",
  "block.fantasy_furniture.wooden_sofa": "Wooden Sofa",
  "block.fantasy_furniture.bookshelf_1": "Bookshelf Type 1",
  "block.fantasy_furniture.bookshelf_2": "Bookshelf Type 2",
  "item.fantasy_furniture.book": "Book",
  "block.fantasy_furniture.eaves_chime": "Wind Chime",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.green_sofa": "Right-click to set it down. It is three blocks wide. Right-click to sit. You cannot recolor it with a brush, and it has no storage. Breaking it drops one green sofa.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.banquette": "Right-click to set it down. Next to another banquette, it turns into a straight piece or a left or right corner by itself.$(br)Right-click to sit. You cannot recolor it with a brush, and it has no storage.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.drinkware": "Right-click the ground to set one down. Hold the same color and right-click a placed cup to stack it, up to four high. A different color will not stack. Creative mode does not use up cups when stacking.$(br)Right-click with a brush to change the color. The nine looks are on the next page. You can also put them in or take them out of a cabinet slot. Breaking the stack drops one cup of that color for each layer.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.eaves_chime": "Hold the chime and right-click to hang it. Right-click with a brush to change the color; you can still recolor it after the words are locked.$(br)Right-click an unlocked chime to write on it: two lines, up to sixteen characters each, in the same letters as a sign. Hold a honeycomb and right-click a written chime to lock the words. After that they cannot be changed. Breaking it drops one chime of the same color.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.tanghulu": "Swing it like a wooden sword. It barely hurts. It does nothing else.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.arcane_wand": "Hold use to start the wave: one opening swing, then it keeps repeating. Let go and it finishes the swing it is on, then plays the ending once.$(br)Letting go does not cut the current swing short. There is no other spell yet, and it uses nothing up.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.ceramic_tile": "Hold a brush and right-click this placed tile. The color steps through pink, yellow, blue, green, cyan, purple, then back to pink. A pickaxe breaks it faster.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.window_0": "Right-click this placed window with an empty hand to switch its shape: straight, 45°, 22.5°, 90°, then the angled one. The color stays. Right-click with a brush to change only the color. The shape and facing stay.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.window_open4": "Right-click this placed window with an empty hand to switch between closed and the open angles. The color stays. Right-click with a brush to change only the color. The shape and facing stay.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.window_7": "This window only has the closed shape for now. Right-click with a brush to change only the color. The facing stays.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.stairs": "Right-click to set it down. It takes one block, and it faces the way you are looking. You can walk up the step. You cannot recolor it with a brush, and it has no storage. An axe is the better tool. Breaking it drops this piece.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.cabinet_1": "Place one block at a time, up to three high. Cabinets beside each other that face the same way lose the wall where they meet. Right-click while holding an item to put it in this compartment; items can stack inside. If it will not fit, you see “Not enough space in the cabinet.” Sneak and right-click the item inside to take it out. The Fantasy Debug Stick can remove or restore the middle divider; with it gone, the upper and lower compartments open into one space and items can stack across them. The four looks are on the next page.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.cabinet_2": "It is one block tall. The front is a three-by-three grid under your crosshair: click a cell to put one item there. A cell that already has something will not take another. Right-click a filled cell with an empty hand to turn the item 45 degrees. Sneak and right-click the item to take it out. If you are sneaking, holding a block, and not aiming at an item inside, the block is placed normally instead of going into the cabinet. Breaking the cabinet spills what is inside. The six looks are on the next page.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.bed_plate6": "Hold it and right-click the ground to set it down. This is a double bed and takes two blocks. You must put a sheet on first before a cover or pillows. With a sheet, landing on it is soft; without one, you do not bounce. The crosshair can pick the bed and each layer on it separately. Aim the Fantasy Spool at a layer to change its color. The disassembly glove on the sheet also takes the cover and every pillow.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.bed_plate1": "Hold it and right-click the ground to set it down. It is two by two, and one person can sleep on each side. Without a sheet you do not bounce, and fall damage is not reduced; with a sheet, landing is soft. The sheet is optional. If you add bedding, sheet first, then the cover, then pillows. The crosshair can pick the bed and each layer separately. To remove a layer, hold the disassembly glove and aim at that layer.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.bed_plate2": "Hold it and right-click the ground to set it down. It is one block wide and two long. The sheet is optional. A long pillow cannot share the bed with a sheet or cover: put the long pillow on first and you cannot add a sheet or cover; put the bedding on first and you cannot add the long pillow. The crosshair can pick the bed and each layer separately. To remove a layer, hold the disassembly glove and aim at that layer.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.bed_plate3": "Hold it and right-click the ground to set it down. It is one block wide and two long. The sheet is optional. If you add bedding, sheet first, then the cover, then pillows. This is not a double bed: no long pillow and no blanket. The crosshair can pick the bed and each layer separately. To remove a layer, hold the disassembly glove and aim at that layer.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.bed_plate4": "Hold it and right-click the ground to set it down. It is one block wide and two long. The sheet is optional. If you add bedding, sheet first, then the cover, then pillows. This is not a double bed: no long pillow and no blanket. The crosshair can pick the bed and each layer separately. To remove a layer, hold the disassembly glove and aim at that layer.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.bed_sheet": "Hold it and right-click a placed bed to put it on. The shape follows whichever bed you use. Bed plate 6 needs the sheet before a cover or pillows. The disassembly glove on the sheet also takes the cover and every pillow. On bed plate 6, aim the Fantasy Spool at this layer to change its color.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.bed_sheet_cover": "Once a sheet is on, hold this and right-click to lay it over the sheet. Bed plate 6 needs the sheet first. To take it off, hold the disassembly glove and aim at this layer.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.pillow_large": "Right-click a placed bed to put this large pillow in an empty spot. Bed plate 6 needs a sheet first. To take it off, hold the disassembly glove and aim at this pillow.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.pillow_medium": "Right-click a placed bed to put this medium pillow in an empty spot. Bed plate 6 needs a sheet first. To take it off, hold the disassembly glove and aim at this pillow.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.pillow_small": "Right-click a placed bed to put this small pillow in an empty spot. Bed plate 6 needs a sheet first. To take it off, hold the disassembly glove and aim at this pillow.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.computer": "Right-click to set it down. It starts closed. Right-click with an empty hand to open or close it; right-clicking while holding something else does not.$(br)When open it gives off a little light. Right-click with a brush to change among six colors. The looks are on the next page. Pick-block copies the current color. Breaking it drops that color; open or closed is not kept on the drop.",
  "patchouli.reverie_core.handbook.entry.wallpaper": "Hold a brush and right-click this placed piece. The look steps through pink wallpaper, red, yellow, yellow wainscot, blue, green, purple, then back to pink. A hoe breaks it faster.",
